The Iron Man Mark XLVII (47) suit features prominently in Spider-Man: Homecoming, serving as Tony Stark’s primary armor while acting as a mentor to Peter Parker. Visually homage-ing Ultimate Iron Man from the comics, the suit stands out for its bold aesthetic shift, swapping out much of the traditional gold for prominent silver-grey metallic plating across the torso and legs while maintaining red on the chest, helmet, and extremities. Engineered with ultra-advanced Wi-Fi and satellite telepresence capabilities, the Mark XLVII allows Tony to control the entire suit seamlessly via remote link from halfway across the world—such as when he rescues Peter from a lake while lounging in India—while also housing a fleet of deployable micro-drones that can weld massive structures like a split Staten Island Ferry back together in seconds.
